WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.049
[theme song playing]

00:07.132 --> 00:09.885
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.053 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.145
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.229 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:26.652
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:30.906
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.740 --> 00:35.911
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.994 --> 00:39.581
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.665 --> 00:43.544
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.627 --> 00:45.003
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:45.087 --> 00:45.963
[song concludes]

00:47.256 --> 00:50.842
[Ho-su's father in Korean]
Ho-su. Doesn't your neck hurt?

00:50.926 --> 00:52.177
DESTINATION
IAN MEMORIAL PARK

00:52.261 --> 00:53.178
[chuckles]

00:53.262 --> 00:55.681
I guess this attitude
is typical of an eighth grader.

00:55.764 --> 00:58.767
You're not even responding.
I'm going to tell your mom later.

00:59.351 --> 01:00.352
Which mom?

01:06.775 --> 01:07.776
Ho-su.

01:09.486 --> 01:12.197
Someday, you're also
going to make someone miserable.

01:14.866 --> 01:18.161
There will definitely be a moment

01:18.245 --> 01:20.664
when you cause the person
by your side to lose.

01:20.747 --> 01:22.124
But you know, Ho-su…

01:23.041 --> 01:26.545
Love isn't about winning or losing.
It's about--

01:27.045 --> 01:29.214
[tires squealing]

01:30.549 --> 01:33.135
[doctor] You've been through a lot, Ho-su.

01:34.636 --> 01:36.221
But in my opinion,

01:36.305 --> 01:39.182
it's pointless for him
to have any more surgeries.

01:40.267 --> 01:42.102
What do you mean, Doctor?

01:42.185 --> 01:43.270
[pensive music playing]

01:43.353 --> 01:44.813
We should still do everything we can--

01:44.896 --> 01:45.772
[doctor] Ma'am.

01:45.856 --> 01:48.317
You recall Ho-su's condition
right after the accident, don't you?

01:48.400 --> 01:52.404
Just the fact that he's alive
and walking again is a miracle.

01:53.447 --> 01:56.491
It's time for Ho-su
and the rest of us to face the truth.

01:57.034 --> 02:00.162
Ho-su will never fully recover
from the accident.

02:00.245 --> 02:02.247
There are ducks here!

02:02.331 --> 02:04.374
- Did it swim away? Where is it?
- Hey, a duck!

02:04.458 --> 02:05.709
- It's a duck.
- A duck.

02:05.792 --> 02:06.793
Yes, really.

02:06.877 --> 02:10.547
[doctor] The best we can do right now
is to maintain his current condition.

02:10.631 --> 02:12.466
He can't run.

02:12.549 --> 02:16.845
He should avoid any strenuous exercise.
No hiking, no long walks.

02:17.929 --> 02:18.972
[music concludes]

02:19.056 --> 02:21.475
[teacher] The hike up Dusonbong Peak
before becoming seniors,

02:21.558 --> 02:25.520
the biggest event of your lives,
has been our long-standing tradition.

02:25.604 --> 02:28.690
- Mi-ji, want to race to the top?
- [teacher] To train your body and mind…

02:28.774 --> 02:31.360
- Winner gets 10,000 won. Deal?
- …and your dedication to studying…

02:31.443 --> 02:32.736
- Jeez.
- …at your final crossroads.

02:32.819 --> 02:35.072
Is it really okay for me
to keep taking your money?

02:35.155 --> 02:37.366
- [young Seung-hyeon scoffs]
- You wanna bet?

02:37.449 --> 02:39.493
[teacher] …so you can soar even higher…

02:39.576 --> 02:41.703
Don't fool around and get hurt.

02:41.787 --> 02:45.123
We'll be checking
to see if all of you reach the top.

02:45.207 --> 02:47.793
Don't try to cheat by coming down
before reaching the top.

02:47.876 --> 02:49.086
[students] Yes, sir.

02:49.169 --> 02:51.380
Those who aren't feeling well are exempt.

02:51.880 --> 02:54.675
You can stay over there
with the school nurse.

02:59.346 --> 03:01.473
[pensive music playing]

03:01.556 --> 03:03.850
Are you sure
they're not exempt for being smart?

03:03.934 --> 03:04.810
[whistle blows]

03:04.893 --> 03:05.894
Get going!

03:05.977 --> 03:08.730
[students chattering]

03:18.490 --> 03:19.950
[Mi-rae] Where are you going?

03:22.202 --> 03:23.203
Dusonbong Peak.

03:24.037 --> 03:25.664
What for?

03:27.499 --> 03:29.459
You're being self-absorbed.

03:30.711 --> 03:33.130
No one cares
whether we go up there or not.

03:33.213 --> 03:34.881
Stop making a big deal out of it.

03:37.134 --> 03:39.386
- [birds chirping]
- [pensive music continues]

03:46.393 --> 03:47.561
[Mi-ji] Ho-su!

03:49.771 --> 03:51.022
[music fades]

03:53.734 --> 03:55.068
I'm surprised you're here.

03:56.445 --> 03:59.030
Are you also going to the top
to wish for good CSAT results?

03:59.114 --> 04:00.073
[pants]

04:01.074 --> 04:02.617
Why did you come back down?

04:02.701 --> 04:06.371
The others said you were coming up,
so I wanted to see for myself.

04:07.456 --> 04:08.665
Do you want some water?

04:08.749 --> 04:10.459
DUSONBONG PEAK
NOKYEONG WATERFALL

04:11.209 --> 04:13.670
Hey, do you want to use this?
It seems useful.

04:14.254 --> 04:16.882
Hey, hiking is all about the gear.
Here you go.

04:21.970 --> 04:25.348
What's going on?
You already reached the top?

04:25.432 --> 04:26.892
No, I'm just running away.

04:26.975 --> 04:29.811
Seung-hyeon is at the top right now,
and he said no one is checking.

04:29.895 --> 04:30.979
[pants]

04:31.062 --> 04:32.981
Mi-ji, if you don't hurry,
you're gonna be last.

04:33.064 --> 04:34.065
Okay.

04:38.069 --> 04:39.029
Go on ahead.

04:39.112 --> 04:41.573
No, I don't want to break a sweat
when I'm not even training.

04:42.199 --> 04:43.074
Just go.

04:43.158 --> 04:45.076
It's fine. Let's go together.

04:45.160 --> 04:46.953
Please just go!

04:47.496 --> 04:48.622
[pants]

04:48.705 --> 04:50.749
[soft pensive music playing]

04:50.832 --> 04:52.876
[pants heavily, mutters] Damn it.

04:55.128 --> 04:58.215
[Mi-ji] Your first love is Mi-ji?

04:58.298 --> 04:59.883
[soft pensive music continues]

04:59.966 --> 05:02.010
Why are you acting all surprised?

05:02.636 --> 05:03.929
I thought you knew.

05:04.763 --> 05:05.764
I did?

05:06.473 --> 05:08.016
But you definitely…

05:08.725 --> 05:10.268
Wait. Since when?

05:10.352 --> 05:12.270
What do you mean?

05:12.354 --> 05:15.398
No one decides when to start
falling in love for the first time.

05:15.482 --> 05:20.529
You must have some idea
of when or why you fell for her.

05:21.446 --> 05:22.489
Dusonbong Peak.

05:22.572 --> 05:23.907
Dusonbong Peak? The mountain?

05:23.990 --> 05:24.866
[music fades]

05:24.950 --> 05:26.910
You mean the one the whole school hiked?

05:26.993 --> 05:29.621
- [cell phone buzzing]
- Yes, if I had to pick a time.

05:29.704 --> 05:31.039
- Hey…
- [soft quirky music playing]

05:31.122 --> 05:33.250
Hold on. Hello?

05:34.709 --> 05:36.169
Yes, I'll be right there.

05:36.253 --> 05:37.420
Oh… [sighs]

05:39.047 --> 05:40.257
[cell phone beeps]

05:40.340 --> 05:42.175
- That mountain--
- Let's go.

05:42.259 --> 05:43.468
Wait. Hey!

05:45.720 --> 05:49.099
Wow. Dusonbong Peak? Me?

05:49.724 --> 05:52.227
Me? Seriously?

05:52.310 --> 05:53.603
EPISODE 5
ALONE WITH YOU

05:56.231 --> 05:58.441
[music concludes]

06:03.280 --> 06:04.656
HO-SU

06:04.739 --> 06:08.076
[sighs] The more I think about it,
the weirder it is.

06:08.159 --> 06:09.786
He liked Mi-rae, though.

06:09.870 --> 06:11.079
[soft intriguing music playing]

06:11.162 --> 06:14.082
You came, though.
You came and left with Mi-rae.

06:14.708 --> 06:16.251
- Am I wrong?
- You're right.

06:16.960 --> 06:18.336
[Mi-ji] That's what he said.

06:18.420 --> 06:20.213
Why is he suddenly claiming
I'm his first love?

06:20.297 --> 06:21.840
SINCE WHEN? JEALOUSY?

06:21.923 --> 06:25.093
Don't tell me he's trying
to make Mi-rae jealous.

06:25.176 --> 06:26.136
[inhales]

06:26.219 --> 06:28.346
And what's with Dusonbong Peak?

06:28.430 --> 06:31.099
[sighs] I can't even ask him outright
what he meant.

06:32.267 --> 06:34.603
[Tae-gwan] This is the Planning
Coordination Department.

06:34.686 --> 06:36.062
[music concludes]

06:37.606 --> 06:39.065
The Digital Innovation Team.

06:39.149 --> 06:40.483
[team 1] Hello.

06:40.567 --> 06:42.068
[Tae-gwan]
The Corporate Relations Team.

06:42.152 --> 06:43.153
[team 2] Hello.

06:43.236 --> 06:45.655
And this is the Planning Strategy Team.

06:47.741 --> 06:50.285
What are you waiting for?
Say hello to the CEO.

06:50.368 --> 06:51.745
[team 3] Hello, sir.

06:51.828 --> 06:54.372
Is this the team in charge
of the new HQ project?

06:54.456 --> 06:57.417
Yes, our team is taking care
of all the minor tasks,

06:57.500 --> 06:59.711
such as securing the site
before the construction--

06:59.794 --> 07:01.504
The site issue isn't a minor task.

07:02.130 --> 07:04.424
Yes, you're right.
Every task is important. I--

07:04.966 --> 07:06.426
No, they're not all important.

07:07.052 --> 07:09.554
[suspenseful music playing]

07:09.638 --> 07:11.222
[chuckles]

07:11.306 --> 07:13.391
I'm just spouting nonsense
because I don't know much.

07:13.475 --> 07:15.852
As you all know,
I don't come from a public corporation,

07:15.936 --> 07:19.314
so I'm not up-to-date on the new HQ
and how things work around here.

07:19.397 --> 07:20.482
- Mr. Shin.
- Yes, sir.

07:20.565 --> 07:23.109
You didn't give him a separate report
on the new HQ project?

07:23.193 --> 07:24.527
Ms. Yu, is the report ready yet?

07:26.363 --> 07:27.489
Pardon?

07:29.574 --> 07:31.534
I'm sorry. The employee in charge is--

07:31.618 --> 07:34.621
It's my fault, sir. I'll tell them
to get it ready as soon as possible.

07:34.704 --> 07:35.747
Okay, then.

07:35.830 --> 07:37.082
Good work, everyone.

07:37.165 --> 07:38.500
[employee] Thank you, sir.

07:43.505 --> 07:45.215
[music concludes]

07:45.298 --> 07:47.842
Mi-rae. You heard him, right?

07:47.926 --> 07:50.053
Get the project report ready by next week.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.390
Pardon?

07:53.473 --> 07:54.975
- Sir.
- [quirky music playing]

07:55.058 --> 07:58.186
I can't make a project report
by myself in just a few days.

07:58.269 --> 08:01.773
Come on. That report should be
a piece of cake for you.

08:01.856 --> 08:04.901
Then can you at least assign
one more person to help?

08:04.985 --> 08:07.445
You joined this project knowing
it was confidential, didn't you?

08:07.529 --> 08:08.697
- But…
- Well?

08:08.780 --> 08:10.865
Why did you accept it in the first place?

08:11.491 --> 08:13.952
Wasn't it because you wanted
the reward all for yourself?

08:14.035 --> 08:16.287
So do the work by yourself.

08:18.123 --> 08:20.000
If you can't, then say so.

08:20.083 --> 08:21.793
The penalty will be all yours too.

08:27.382 --> 08:29.801
[Mi-ji breathes deeply]

08:30.760 --> 08:32.345
[whimpers]

08:33.388 --> 08:35.849
- [music concludes]
- [Se-jin] It looks so pretty.

08:35.932 --> 08:39.310
How should I repay you
for giving me such a precious gift?

08:39.394 --> 08:41.646
What goes well with strawberry jam?

08:41.730 --> 08:43.898
Scones! I should make scones.

08:43.982 --> 08:45.442
Let's get the scone ingredients first!

08:45.525 --> 08:47.027
But we… [sighs]

08:54.743 --> 08:56.411
You're lasting a pretty long time.

08:56.494 --> 08:59.497
At this rate, this strawberry farm job
is going to be your longest gig.

08:59.581 --> 09:00.582
Right.

09:00.665 --> 09:04.586
Getting paid 200,000 won a day
is a pretty sweet deal.

09:05.336 --> 09:08.256
But what if you were offered a job
that pays 250,000 won right now?

09:08.339 --> 09:10.258
We're organizing our warehouse next week.

09:10.341 --> 09:11.926
Plus, it's not just for a day.

09:12.010 --> 09:14.012
Four days!
That's a total of one million won.

09:14.095 --> 09:15.138
[cheers]

09:18.349 --> 09:19.976
What's with that reaction?

09:20.518 --> 09:23.730
Did your blood sugar just spike
because the offer was too sweet?

09:23.813 --> 09:26.149
Oh, me?

09:26.232 --> 09:27.692
You want me to organize the warehouse?

09:27.776 --> 09:30.070
So should I pay myself to organize it?

09:30.153 --> 09:31.446
Put your muscles to good use.

09:31.529 --> 09:33.615
Oh, but…

09:34.324 --> 09:37.827
it's a really important time
for the strawberries right now.

09:37.911 --> 09:39.621
What do you mean?

09:39.704 --> 09:42.791
So you're turning down a job
that pays 250,000 won a day?

09:42.874 --> 09:44.250
Are you really Mi-ji?

09:45.418 --> 09:49.047
I would love to organize the warehouse.

09:49.130 --> 09:52.050
But I need to finish up
what I started, so--

09:52.133 --> 09:54.135
What's with that pointless sense
of responsibility?

09:54.219 --> 09:55.386
It's just a temporary job.

09:55.470 --> 09:57.889
[Se-jin] "It's just a temporary job"?

09:57.972 --> 09:58.848
[quirky music playing]

09:58.932 --> 10:02.393
Did you miss the village chief's warning
about not poaching other people's workers?

10:02.477 --> 10:07.232
Why do you keep sticking your nose
where it doesn't belong?

10:07.816 --> 10:11.402
And you stole my worker first.

10:11.486 --> 10:13.780
She almost became our store's
assistant deputy manager.

10:13.863 --> 10:16.032
That's a ridiculous job title.

10:16.116 --> 10:17.992
Why are there so many job titles anyway?

10:18.076 --> 10:19.994
Plus, she's my business partner.

10:20.078 --> 10:21.871
Your "business partner."

10:22.789 --> 10:26.960
- Are you willing to give her some land?
- I can. Can you?

10:27.043 --> 10:28.169
Did you get one of these?

10:28.253 --> 10:30.505
- What is that?
- [in English] Oops.

10:31.297 --> 10:33.216
[in Korean]
My business partner made this herself.

10:33.299 --> 10:36.052
It's 100% handmade strawberry jam.

10:36.678 --> 10:39.305
As of now, I refuse to talk to anyone
who didn't receive one.

10:39.389 --> 10:40.598
- [zipper closing]
- [fast squeak]

10:40.682 --> 10:41.850
[chuckles]

10:41.933 --> 10:43.434
Are you saying she made this…

10:44.018 --> 10:45.061
For him?

10:47.647 --> 10:50.984
Mi-ji! That's not right.

10:51.067 --> 10:53.820
You can't do this to me.

10:53.903 --> 10:56.781
I just made it with the strawberries
from the farm, though.

10:56.865 --> 10:59.742
But you've never made
anything like this for me.

10:59.826 --> 11:02.745
Make me one too.
Make one using our store's strawberries!

11:02.829 --> 11:05.415
- [Se-jin] We're in public. Quiet down.
- [Gyeong-gu] Make me one too!

11:05.498 --> 11:07.167
[music concludes]

11:10.962 --> 11:12.422
[doctor] No, please don't get up.

11:12.505 --> 11:13.548
[Ro-sa groans]

11:13.631 --> 11:14.549
[doctor inhales]

11:14.632 --> 11:18.136
Fortunately, there's nothing wrong
with your head or your bones.

11:18.219 --> 11:22.265
Ma'am, have you ever been sick before?

11:23.349 --> 11:25.101
[hesitates] Pardon?

11:25.185 --> 11:27.145
You must've been in pain.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.314
Did you have severe abdominal pain…

11:29.397 --> 11:31.274
- Well…
- …or indigestion?

11:31.357 --> 11:35.320
- [soft pensive music playing]
- If you're talking about

11:35.403 --> 11:37.655
the stomach issue I had
when I was younger…

11:37.739 --> 11:39.866
Oh no! Ro-sa!

11:39.949 --> 11:41.826
Ro-sa, are you okay? Oh dear…

11:41.910 --> 11:44.537
[shouting]
Why is no one coming here to help her?

11:44.621 --> 11:48.041
No, I just saw some gallstones on your CT.

11:48.958 --> 11:50.752
- Gallstones?
- [doctor] Yes.

11:50.835 --> 11:53.588
I saw quite a few.

11:53.671 --> 11:57.592
With this many gallstones,
the pain must've been unbearable.

11:57.675 --> 11:59.552
Haven't you gone to see a doctor?

11:59.636 --> 12:01.930
Oh, I…

12:02.513 --> 12:06.059
I just thought it was due to old age.

12:07.852 --> 12:09.354
[breathes deeply]

12:09.437 --> 12:11.898
[woman sobbing]
Ro-sa, hang in there just a little longer.

12:11.981 --> 12:13.024
[breathes shakily]

12:13.107 --> 12:14.317
[Ro-sa groans]

12:15.860 --> 12:17.487
- Surgery?
- [music fades]

12:18.529 --> 12:21.741
They found gallstones
while doing a pelvic CT scan.

12:22.242 --> 12:25.286
So she would've never known
if she hadn't hurt her back.

12:25.370 --> 12:26.996
Hey, this is totally…

12:28.373 --> 12:29.582
A disguise something…

12:29.666 --> 12:32.126
Yes, a blessing in disguise.

12:32.210 --> 12:34.671
It's not a major surgery,
so I got the earliest date possible.

12:34.754 --> 12:37.215
Your friend is also very stubborn.

12:38.091 --> 12:39.926
I told him it's fine, but he kept…

12:40.009 --> 12:41.886
You're not okay.
You were just enduring it.

12:41.970 --> 12:43.638
- Gosh.
- He's right.

12:43.721 --> 12:45.181
You also hurt your back,

12:45.265 --> 12:47.267
so just focus on your recovery
until the surgery.

12:47.350 --> 12:50.144
You two make a great team.

12:51.145 --> 12:53.564
Anyway, given my current situation,

12:53.648 --> 12:58.403
he'll have to go alone
to that meeting we talked about.

12:58.486 --> 13:00.738
It'll be easier
than dealing with an old lady

13:00.822 --> 13:03.032
who doesn't know anything.

13:04.117 --> 13:06.411
So when should I tell my company
you're available?

13:06.494 --> 13:08.997
It doesn't matter to me.
Choose a day that works for you.

13:09.080 --> 13:10.290
A day that works for me?

13:11.958 --> 13:14.836
Then let me ask my team leader and…

13:14.919 --> 13:17.088
Never mind. I'll just call him myself.

13:17.714 --> 13:18.631
Why?

13:18.715 --> 13:21.384
He might yell at you
since you're in the middle of it all.

13:21.467 --> 13:23.553
We're the ones rescheduling,
so I'll tell him.

13:23.636 --> 13:25.138
I can call your team leader, right?

13:25.221 --> 13:26.764
- [Mi-ji] See?
- [quirky music playing]

13:26.848 --> 13:29.726
[Mi-ji] He's making it so obvious
that he still likes Mi-rae.

13:29.809 --> 13:31.436
Why is he pretending otherwise?

13:31.519 --> 13:33.604
[scoffs] First love, my butt.

13:36.149 --> 13:37.984
Why are you looking at me like that?

13:40.945 --> 13:42.363
Why Dusonbong Peak?

13:42.447 --> 13:43.573
- What?
- [music concludes]

13:43.656 --> 13:47.076
I kept thinking about it
after what you told me.

13:47.160 --> 13:50.121
Nothing special really happened
at Dusonbong Peak

13:51.122 --> 13:52.457
for you to have fallen for her.

13:52.540 --> 13:53.833
You wouldn't know.

13:54.459 --> 13:57.295
You stayed at the foot
of the mountain instead of hiking.

13:58.546 --> 14:00.673
But I saw the two of you come down.

14:00.757 --> 14:02.800
- [young Mi-ji grunts]
- [intriguing music playing]

14:02.884 --> 14:05.636
Mi-ji! Ho-su! You brats!

14:05.720 --> 14:08.765
- What took you so long?
- [Mi-ji] Everyone was back except you two.

14:08.848 --> 14:11.851
You showed up right before
the teachers went looking for you.

14:15.063 --> 14:18.733
Did you start liking her
because she helped you come down?

14:18.816 --> 14:21.235
Mi-ji practically carried you down
on her back.

14:21.319 --> 14:23.529
Was it because of a sense
of camaraderie or solidarity?

14:23.613 --> 14:25.323
It happened when we were going up.

14:25.907 --> 14:27.116
What?

14:27.200 --> 14:30.203
I fell in love with her on the way up,
not coming down.

14:32.288 --> 14:34.457
Anyway, I'll call you after we set a date.

14:38.920 --> 14:42.256
What is he talking about?
He went up by himself.

14:42.340 --> 14:43.383
[music concludes]

14:43.466 --> 14:45.009
What could it be?

14:45.093 --> 14:46.719
HOW TO WRITE A PROJECT REPORT

14:46.803 --> 14:48.221
[Mi-ji] There are so many places

14:48.304 --> 14:51.224
that offer to write papers
and personal statements for a fee.

14:51.307 --> 14:53.768
So why aren't there any places
that write reports?

14:53.851 --> 14:56.354
Why is no one willing to write it? Jeez!

14:56.437 --> 14:57.688
[inhales deeply]

14:58.189 --> 14:59.148
[exhales]

15:01.067 --> 15:04.112
She threw a fit just over the meeting.

15:04.195 --> 15:08.032
As soon as I mention the project report,
Mi-rae is going to kill me!

15:08.116 --> 15:11.285
[Mi-rae] Just stay put
and don't do anything.

15:11.369 --> 15:12.829
[cries]

15:12.912 --> 15:16.624
Jeez! I'm so screwed!

15:16.707 --> 15:18.376
What am I going to do?

15:19.419 --> 15:21.087
Should I just write whatever I can?

15:21.170 --> 15:25.758
But I need to know the basics
in order to write anything at all.

15:25.842 --> 15:28.344
Damn it! I'm so screwed.

15:28.428 --> 15:31.305
I'm seriously screwed.
What am I going to do?

15:31.389 --> 15:33.474
[cell phone buzzing]

15:33.558 --> 15:35.601
MI-JI

15:37.520 --> 15:39.730
- What?
- [Mi-rae] You're alone now, right?

15:40.481 --> 15:41.691
Why?

15:41.774 --> 15:44.819
Grandma wants to hear your voice.
Talk to her for a minute.

15:44.902 --> 15:46.696
Grandma, I'll go get more blankets.

15:47.321 --> 15:48.364
Grandma!

15:49.323 --> 15:52.827
Goodness, you're going to make
my ears fall off.

15:52.910 --> 15:56.122
Why did you suddenly become a baby?

15:56.205 --> 15:58.291
Grandma, is Mi-rae doing a good job?

15:58.374 --> 16:00.626
Are you okay?
Wait. Did you get your haircut?

16:00.710 --> 16:05.214
[chuckling] Goodness, slow down.

16:05.756 --> 16:07.925
Everything is good here.

16:08.009 --> 16:10.136
Are you doing okay over there?

16:11.012 --> 16:13.306
No, I'm not okay.

16:13.931 --> 16:16.893
I don't know
what I'm doing here right now.

16:16.976 --> 16:20.146
I don't know how to do anything,
but things keep happening.

16:20.229 --> 16:23.357
I'm living on edge every day.
[breathes deeply]

16:23.441 --> 16:24.609
Mi-ji.

16:25.526 --> 16:29.822
Do you remember the promise we made?

16:30.323 --> 16:32.992
- [tender music playing]
- [Wol-sun] Even though you're not here,

16:33.075 --> 16:36.037
I'm holding up my end of the promise.

16:36.829 --> 16:39.040
You will too, right?

16:39.123 --> 16:41.209
- Whatever.
- [Wol-sun chuckles]

16:41.292 --> 16:45.129
Don't ever forget our promise.

16:46.047 --> 16:48.466
I'll call you again.

16:49.926 --> 16:50.927
[cell phone beeps]

16:56.140 --> 16:57.892
[tender music continues]

17:00.728 --> 17:01.854
What promise?

17:03.397 --> 17:05.107
It's a secret.

17:07.818 --> 17:08.861
Jeez.

17:09.570 --> 17:11.572
You two always have secrets of your own.

17:14.033 --> 17:15.701
- [music fades]
- [paper crunching]

17:21.707 --> 17:22.750
KFMC

17:22.833 --> 17:24.752
REFERENCE DOCUMENTS FOR THE NEW HQ

17:24.835 --> 17:27.171
[soft intriguing music playing]

17:36.764 --> 17:38.849
Tae-i, do you have
the documents I requested?

17:38.933 --> 17:40.142
AESIM-DONG LAND LOT SIZE REPORT

17:40.226 --> 17:41.978
[Tae-i] I'm doing them in order.

17:42.603 --> 17:45.022
Tae-i, can you do mine first?

17:45.106 --> 17:47.692
I have to submit this
to the audit office, so I'm in a rush.

17:47.775 --> 17:49.777
I'll do them in order.

17:51.737 --> 17:52.989
Where are you going?

17:53.072 --> 17:55.575
Oh, it's lunchtime.

17:55.658 --> 17:56.784
[employee 1] Ah.

17:58.452 --> 18:00.288
[music fades]

18:00.371 --> 18:03.708
[employee 2] Look at how he talks.
AI is probably more human than he is.

18:03.791 --> 18:05.251
We hired him as a contract worker,

18:05.334 --> 18:08.671
but he's acting all high-and-mighty
just because he's a data analyst!

18:08.754 --> 18:11.716
He's telling us to do it ourselves
if we don't like it.

18:11.799 --> 18:13.217
There's nothing we can do.

18:13.301 --> 18:16.637
He can generate data in just a few hours,
whereas it would take us days to do it.

18:16.721 --> 18:18.431
Beggars can't be choosers.

18:18.514 --> 18:19.807
[intriguing music playing]

18:19.890 --> 18:22.268
Are you okay? I'll do it.

18:23.144 --> 18:24.186
[Mi-ji] Pardon?

18:24.270 --> 18:27.189
I'll finish getting things ready here.
You go check on her.

18:29.942 --> 18:32.111
[intriguing music continues]

18:49.170 --> 18:51.213
It was you, right?

18:51.297 --> 18:52.423
Pardon?

18:52.506 --> 18:55.843
You left this for me, didn't you?

18:59.055 --> 19:02.141
But I never asked you to do it.

19:02.224 --> 19:04.977
So why did you do it
before everyone else's requests?

19:06.979 --> 19:10.066
The CEO visited us recently,
so it seemed more urgent.

19:10.149 --> 19:12.985
But you don't seem to prioritize things
solely based on urgency.

19:13.069 --> 19:14.403
You do them in order.

19:16.030 --> 19:17.156
[sighs]

19:17.239 --> 19:19.533
What are you trying to say?

19:23.996 --> 19:25.414
[whispers] Please help me.

19:26.999 --> 19:28.542
- I can't.
- [music concludes]

19:28.626 --> 19:31.337
I've never even written a report before.
How am I supposed--

19:31.420 --> 19:33.506
I'm not asking you
to write the report for me.

19:33.589 --> 19:35.675
If you just continue to help me
with things like this--

19:35.758 --> 19:38.010
If you need documents, then request them.

19:38.594 --> 19:41.305
You keep saying I helped you,
but providing documents is my job.

19:41.389 --> 19:43.307
I wasn't going out of my way to help you.

19:43.391 --> 19:44.809
You did help me.

19:44.892 --> 19:48.604
You asked me if I was okay,
and you did my work for me.

19:48.688 --> 19:50.981
[sighs] So…

19:51.691 --> 19:54.568
why did you take on this project
after laying low all this time?

19:54.652 --> 19:57.029
Do you even know
who's in charge of the new HQ?

19:57.113 --> 19:58.364
I…

19:58.447 --> 20:01.575
I think I heard it was Mr. Park.

20:01.659 --> 20:04.537
You accepted this project
knowing Mr. Park is in charge?

20:05.621 --> 20:08.958
Anyway, I'm sure you're a pro
when it comes to paperwork.

20:09.041 --> 20:11.085
You've probably written
countless project reports.

20:11.168 --> 20:12.545
So even without my help, you'll--

20:12.628 --> 20:13.713
I can't do it alone.

20:14.463 --> 20:18.467
When someone is forced into a corner,

20:18.551 --> 20:21.053
they become a mess.
They can't function like they usually do.

20:21.137 --> 20:22.763
Don't I sound weird right now?

20:23.389 --> 20:25.391
But you've been doing this for a while.

20:25.474 --> 20:26.642
So I…

20:26.726 --> 20:28.519
I'm sorry, Mi-rae.

20:29.311 --> 20:32.231
To be honest, I'm taking medications,
and I'm getting therapy too.

20:32.314 --> 20:34.984
I cry every day. I can't sleep,
and I also have trouble breathing.

20:35.067 --> 20:37.027
You saw me at the bus stop the other day.

20:37.111 --> 20:40.740
I was sitting there
because I suddenly forgot how to walk.

20:40.823 --> 20:43.200
- [quirky music playing]
- I'm not myself right now.

20:43.284 --> 20:45.369
I really don't want to ask
for a favor like this,

20:45.453 --> 20:47.496
and I know I look weird doing it.

20:47.580 --> 20:50.082
But I really have no one to ask for help.

20:50.166 --> 20:53.377
I mean, I'm asking you
of all people for help.

20:56.547 --> 20:57.548
You just need data?

20:57.631 --> 20:58.758
Yes.

20:59.467 --> 21:01.427
I'll prioritize your data.

21:02.178 --> 21:03.721
Tell me what you need.

21:04.805 --> 21:07.183
Please just give me everything.

21:07.975 --> 21:10.895
What do you mean by "everything"?

21:11.687 --> 21:15.524
Any project reports or documents
that you think seem relevant.

21:15.608 --> 21:17.693
Just give me everything!

21:17.777 --> 21:20.571
Tae-i, are you done with mine yet?
I'm in a rush.

21:20.654 --> 21:22.156
Tae-i, what about mine?

21:22.239 --> 21:24.366
[quirky music continues]

21:29.330 --> 21:30.998
AESIM-DONG 1-GA RESIDENT DEMOGRAPHICS

21:32.625 --> 21:34.585
KPI FEASIBILITY REVIEW
FOR ESG COMPLIANCE

21:34.668 --> 21:35.878
[quirky music continues]

21:36.420 --> 21:38.172
Damn it.

21:39.256 --> 21:40.424
[gasps]

21:40.508 --> 21:43.177
A STUDY ON WAYS TO EXPAND
GREEN SPACES IN REDEVELOPMENT AREAS

21:45.304 --> 21:46.430
TOTAL OF 32 KPIS

21:46.514 --> 21:47.389
"KPI"?

21:48.432 --> 21:49.433
I see.

21:49.517 --> 21:51.101
KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATOR

21:51.185 --> 21:54.104
Given that it was the most critical issue,

21:54.188 --> 21:57.066
we anticipate that
it will positively impact the KPIs too.

21:57.149 --> 21:58.567
KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATOR

21:58.651 --> 22:00.236
Oh, KPI.

22:00.319 --> 22:02.029
[employee] Next is the website management…

22:03.614 --> 22:04.990
KPI.

22:05.074 --> 22:07.034
[quirky music continues]

22:07.117 --> 22:09.787
HOW TO WRITE A TABLE OF CONTENTS
WRITE CONTENT TO MATCH TABLE

22:19.046 --> 22:20.548
TABLE OF CONTENTS

22:21.215 --> 22:22.424
20% OF UNEMPLOYMENT
IS LONG-TERM

22:22.508 --> 22:24.301
Everyone is desperate to get a job.

22:24.385 --> 22:27.763
- [anchor] Twenty percent are unemployed.
- Why would he quit his perfectly good job?

22:27.847 --> 22:29.598
[anchor]
More than half of them are youths…

22:29.682 --> 22:31.141
Who quit?

22:31.225 --> 22:33.561
You didn't hear about it
when you were making jam?

22:33.644 --> 22:36.146
Ho-su quit his job at the law firm.

22:37.481 --> 22:39.400
Ho-su? Why?

22:39.483 --> 22:41.861
How would I know that
when his own mom doesn't?

22:42.611 --> 22:44.029
How could he just suddenly quit

22:44.113 --> 22:46.657
when his mom worked so hard
to support him?

22:46.740 --> 22:50.536
That brat, Bun-hong, used to always brag

22:50.619 --> 22:53.789
about how it's one of the top three
law firms in the country.

22:53.873 --> 22:54.957
[chuckles]

22:55.040 --> 22:57.668
But these days, she's really down.

22:59.003 --> 23:03.173
He must have had a good reason.
Maybe the law firm was the problem.

23:03.257 --> 23:05.843
Even if there was a problem,
it was probably his fault.

23:05.926 --> 23:07.803
You know Ho-su was always like that.

23:09.138 --> 23:10.806
He had a hard time adjusting to school.

23:10.890 --> 23:12.474
He was probably the same at the office.

23:12.558 --> 23:16.270
People who have issues…

23:17.521 --> 23:20.441
always take their issues with them
wherever they go.

23:21.358 --> 23:22.860
Give me that towel.

23:31.368 --> 23:34.246
[Secretary Hwang]
You set up your own firm? Out of the blue?

23:34.872 --> 23:36.206
Where's your office?

23:37.166 --> 23:41.378
I just filed a business registration
to help someone I know.

23:41.462 --> 23:44.548
You? Who is this person?

23:46.175 --> 23:49.970
That crochet lady from before?

23:50.054 --> 23:52.765
I'm telling you,
she and I are just friends.

23:53.432 --> 23:55.434
Your face tells me a different story.

23:56.310 --> 24:00.064
I might receive
a wedding invitation next spring.

24:01.148 --> 24:02.274
[sighs]

24:08.781 --> 24:12.451
She's my first love's twin.

24:14.787 --> 24:15.996
[Secretary Hwang] What?

24:16.080 --> 24:17.331
So you're saying…

24:17.915 --> 24:21.835
that the crochet lady
is your first love's twin?

24:22.753 --> 24:23.921
They look the same?

24:24.546 --> 24:26.423
Yes, they're identical.

24:26.507 --> 24:28.384
Did it work out with your first love?

24:29.176 --> 24:32.179
No, there was nothing like that.
We were just too young.

24:32.805 --> 24:33.889
I see.

24:33.973 --> 24:37.017
You're trying to make it work
with your unrequited first love's twin?

24:37.101 --> 24:39.478
That's a bit strange.

24:39.561 --> 24:41.063
I told you that it's not like that.

24:41.146 --> 24:43.732
There's nothing going on between us,
and I'll make sure it doesn't.

24:43.816 --> 24:45.359
Oh…

24:45.442 --> 24:46.944
You'll make sure it doesn't?

24:47.027 --> 24:49.655
- So there is something between you two.
- There isn't.

24:49.738 --> 24:52.032
So did you ever tell your first love
how you felt?

24:53.158 --> 24:55.995
- No, it was just one-sided.
- Does the crochet lady know?

24:56.078 --> 24:57.788
That her twin was your first love?

25:00.666 --> 25:02.376
- I thought she did.
- Yes.

25:02.459 --> 25:04.837
But now she's acting like she never knew.

25:04.920 --> 25:08.090
That's good.
Then there's nothing stopping you two.

25:08.173 --> 25:10.259
You can go out with the crochet lady now…

25:11.593 --> 25:14.096
Wait. Hold on.

25:15.264 --> 25:18.308
You don't still have feelings
for your first love, do you?

25:19.518 --> 25:21.520
- Pardon?
- [Secretary Hwang] I mean, look at this.

25:21.603 --> 25:24.606
- They look the same.
- [quirky music playing]

25:24.690 --> 25:27.276
[Secretary Hwang]
But you only liked one of them.

25:27.359 --> 25:31.280
She must've been different somehow,
but now you're attracted to the other one.

25:31.905 --> 25:33.490
Has your taste changed?

25:33.991 --> 25:37.828
Or are you looking
for your first love in the other twin?

25:40.164 --> 25:42.416
See, I knew it!

25:42.499 --> 25:45.085
It's important to figure out how you feel.

25:45.169 --> 25:47.588
Things could get weird
if you're not careful.

25:48.797 --> 25:50.215
[clicks tongue] Fine.

25:50.299 --> 25:53.594
At times like this,
there's only one solution.

25:53.677 --> 25:56.847
Since you have nothing to do,
go see for yourself.

25:57.431 --> 25:59.892
Once you see her,
you'll know right away who you like.

25:59.975 --> 26:04.104
[Bun-hong] If you had called me yesterday,
I would've gone grocery shopping.

26:04.188 --> 26:07.399
You came all this way,
but there's not much to eat here.

26:07.483 --> 26:11.236
It's okay.
I'm only here for a short visit.

26:11.820 --> 26:14.740
A short visit? You won't spend the night?

26:15.365 --> 26:17.618
I even cleaned your room.

26:17.701 --> 26:21.497
I have somewhere to go
tomorrow afternoon for work.

26:22.331 --> 26:24.666
I see. You have work.

26:27.127 --> 26:29.797
Why did you buy so much stuff?

26:29.880 --> 26:31.590
You bought two of the same thing.

26:31.673 --> 26:33.550
One is for next door.

26:33.634 --> 26:36.095
Even for your neighbors? My gosh.

26:37.012 --> 26:38.722
- I'll make sure to…
- I'll…

26:39.932 --> 26:42.726
I'll give it to them myself
before I leave.

26:42.810 --> 26:43.727
[quirky music playing]

26:43.811 --> 26:44.853
You will?

26:45.687 --> 26:46.772
Okay.

26:46.855 --> 26:49.108
- [engine pulsing]
- [quirky music continues]

26:51.026 --> 26:53.529
- [engine grinds]
- [Mi-rae] Step on the clutch and--

26:54.238 --> 26:57.699
That's why you should change gears
after you step on the clutch.

27:00.452 --> 27:01.829
[button clicking]

27:03.664 --> 27:05.749
I was surprised
when you asked me for a ride.

27:05.833 --> 27:07.626
Did you want to give me a driving lesson?

27:07.709 --> 27:09.920
There are no tricks or tips
for driving manual.

27:10.003 --> 27:12.172
You just drive every day
and get used to it.

27:14.424 --> 27:15.759
You're so alike.

27:17.511 --> 27:18.595
What do you mean?

27:18.679 --> 27:20.639
I once said you reminded me of someone.

27:21.640 --> 27:24.393
You're just like my grandfather.

27:25.644 --> 27:28.021
- Pardon?
- What's with that reaction?

27:28.897 --> 27:30.691
It is a big compliment.

27:30.774 --> 27:33.360
My grandfather
was my favorite person in the world.

27:35.404 --> 27:36.613
I see.

27:37.322 --> 27:38.699
I mean it.

27:39.491 --> 27:41.410
Grandpa, should I stop over there?

27:44.705 --> 27:46.039
[music concludes]

27:52.838 --> 27:55.174
Well, drive safely.

27:55.257 --> 27:57.009
I will. Oh, wait, the scones!

27:57.092 --> 28:00.137
I got all the ingredients to make scones.

28:00.804 --> 28:04.516
But the oven I ordered has been stuck
at a distribution center for days.

28:05.309 --> 28:07.352
Anyway, as soon as I have an oven,

28:07.436 --> 28:09.980
I'll officially invite you
to an afternoon tea party.

28:10.063 --> 28:13.150
Gosh, it's okay. You don't have to.

28:13.233 --> 28:14.318
[gate closes]

28:15.986 --> 28:17.112
Mi-ji?

28:19.990 --> 28:22.117
[soft music playing]

28:38.967 --> 28:40.427
[music concludes]

28:40.510 --> 28:41.845
You dyed your hair.

28:42.930 --> 28:44.223
It looks good.

28:45.265 --> 28:47.059
Yes, I guess.

28:48.101 --> 28:49.811
So, what brings you here?

28:50.687 --> 28:52.981
I just stopped by my house.

28:55.609 --> 28:58.737
I recently left the firm.

29:01.031 --> 29:02.241
I see.

29:10.707 --> 29:12.376
Who was that earlier?

29:12.459 --> 29:14.419
I've never seen him before.

29:14.503 --> 29:17.673
He's just someone I work with.

29:18.382 --> 29:19.925
Work?

29:20.592 --> 29:21.969
Did you start a new job?

29:22.052 --> 29:25.055
Didn't you say
you had something to tell me?

29:25.597 --> 29:26.598
Oh…

29:27.140 --> 29:28.141
Yes.

29:28.809 --> 29:30.769
It's nothing special.

29:33.355 --> 29:34.690
These days…

29:36.024 --> 29:38.777
I've had a lot of time to think
since I quit my job.

29:39.945 --> 29:42.072
So I've been thinking
a lot about the past.

29:44.157 --> 29:46.910
And it brought back memories
of our time in high school.

29:49.204 --> 29:50.539
By any chance…

29:52.082 --> 29:54.584
do you remember the day
we hiked up Dusonbong Peak?

29:55.127 --> 29:56.128
What?

29:56.670 --> 29:57.921
Dusonbong Peak?

29:58.588 --> 29:59.589
[Ho-su] Yes.

30:02.426 --> 30:03.635
Sometimes…

30:06.054 --> 30:09.308
I still think about the time
we spent together at the top.

30:09.391 --> 30:11.268
[soft daring music playing]

30:11.351 --> 30:14.062
[young Ho-su panting]

30:29.286 --> 30:30.579
[music turns uplifting]

30:30.662 --> 30:31.663
[young Ho-su exhales]

30:42.758 --> 30:44.509
[breathes deeply]

31:04.363 --> 31:07.115
Now that you're here,
there isn't much to see, is there?

31:08.075 --> 31:10.285
So why did you try so hard
to come up here?

31:10.911 --> 31:12.662
[music fades]

31:13.580 --> 31:14.831
Because I don't want to live.

31:16.541 --> 31:17.459
What?

31:18.168 --> 31:19.544
I felt that…

31:21.088 --> 31:23.340
if I couldn't even climb
a mountain like this,

31:24.341 --> 31:25.759
then I would rather die.

31:27.803 --> 31:30.263
[gentle music playing]

31:33.183 --> 31:35.394
Why are you so dramatic?

31:37.020 --> 31:38.480
We should go down now.

31:52.702 --> 31:54.287
[both grunt]

31:56.665 --> 31:57.791
[young Mi-ji] Aren't you hot?

31:58.875 --> 31:59.918
Take it off.

32:04.923 --> 32:06.174
[chuckles softly]

32:08.552 --> 32:13.765
- [gentle pop song playing]
- [singing in Korean]

32:15.559 --> 32:20.439
[singing in Korean continues]

32:23.108 --> 32:27.737
[singing in Korean continues]

32:27.821 --> 32:29.823
- [leaves rustling]
- [wind whistling faintly]

32:29.906 --> 32:34.786
[singing in Korean continues]

32:37.122 --> 32:38.957
[singing in Korean continues]

32:39.040 --> 32:40.709
[Ho-su] Looking back now…

32:43.128 --> 32:45.672
I think that was
a turning point in my life.

32:48.425 --> 32:52.762
If I hadn't made it all the way
to the top that day…

32:55.223 --> 32:57.267
I would be a very different person.

32:59.102 --> 33:02.397
I mean, I'm not saying that
I'm doing exceptionally well right now.

33:02.481 --> 33:04.107
[singing in Korean continues]

33:05.901 --> 33:08.111
But I would've turned out even worse.

33:08.195 --> 33:09.905
So, I know it's late…

33:12.115 --> 33:13.992
but I wanted to thank you.

33:16.661 --> 33:18.580
I went all the way to the top that day…

33:18.663 --> 33:20.749
[singing in Korean continues]

33:23.835 --> 33:25.337
…because of you, Mi-ji.

33:28.340 --> 33:29.508
Because of me?

33:30.842 --> 33:31.760
[Ho-su] Yes.

33:35.055 --> 33:36.056
[Mi-rae] I see.

33:42.354 --> 33:44.731
[song concludes]

33:46.942 --> 33:48.902
[soft quirky music playing]

33:51.905 --> 33:54.741
If you have nothing else to say,
should we get going now?

33:55.992 --> 33:57.327
Okay.

33:59.204 --> 34:00.914
I'm sorry I took up your time.

34:04.584 --> 34:06.461
Oh, and take this.

34:09.005 --> 34:11.466
[soft quirky music continues]

34:18.765 --> 34:20.058
[sighs]

34:20.141 --> 34:22.394
Why does she seem
so different from before?

34:26.856 --> 34:28.024
[music concludes]

34:29.276 --> 34:30.443
I'm off now.

34:31.486 --> 34:33.822
Did I keep you from leaving?

34:34.447 --> 34:36.324
No, I still had work to do.

34:36.408 --> 34:37.617
Oh.

34:40.495 --> 34:41.705
Wait.

34:42.998 --> 34:45.250
Have you eaten yet?

34:46.167 --> 34:48.587
We're all doing this to make a living,

34:48.670 --> 34:50.171
so we should eat well.

34:52.299 --> 34:54.676
That chair's broken. You should sit here.

34:58.972 --> 35:02.517
This project was forced on you,
but I guess you still want to do it.

35:03.810 --> 35:06.104
You look way more comfortable than before.

35:06.187 --> 35:09.190
My gosh, have you been observing me?

35:09.983 --> 35:11.109
Why?

35:12.152 --> 35:14.154
- I'll get going now.
- [Mi-ji] Okay, fine.

35:15.947 --> 35:19.284
Gosh, I was just kidding.
Eat before you go.

35:21.119 --> 35:22.162
Here…

35:23.872 --> 35:25.582
I hope you enjoy it.

35:32.756 --> 35:34.466
Mm. It's good.

35:39.054 --> 35:42.766
I'm really curious, though.

35:43.308 --> 35:45.101
Why are you helping me?

35:46.811 --> 35:49.397
I wasn't going to ask,

35:49.481 --> 35:53.485
but I feel a little uneasy
because you're helping me so much.

35:53.568 --> 35:56.404
- Why do you feel uneasy?
- Because I don't know why you're helping.

35:56.488 --> 36:00.700
I'm wondering if you're a spy
sent by Director Choi.

36:00.784 --> 36:01.826
[scoffs]

36:02.369 --> 36:04.245
Isn't it a little too late
to be suspicious?

36:04.329 --> 36:05.705
You're right.

36:05.789 --> 36:08.833
You're going through
way too much trouble to be a spy.

36:08.917 --> 36:10.001
[chuckles softly]

36:11.086 --> 36:12.712
You helped me before.

36:14.589 --> 36:15.590
Pardon?

36:15.674 --> 36:17.467
You may not remember,

36:17.550 --> 36:20.970
but I owe you a big favor.

36:21.054 --> 36:23.264
[intriguing music playing]

36:25.433 --> 36:28.019
[Mi-ji] Mi-rae, you know Kim Tae-i, right?

36:28.103 --> 36:29.020
STRAWBERRY CULTIVATION

36:29.104 --> 36:30.772
- The actress?
- [Mi-ji] No.

36:30.855 --> 36:33.274
- [music fades]
- Tae-i, not Tae-hee.

36:34.109 --> 36:37.362
You know, that contract worker
on your team?

36:38.655 --> 36:41.783
Oh, that person's name is Kim Tae-i?

36:42.409 --> 36:43.326
So?

36:44.369 --> 36:47.622
Did you ever help him?

36:47.706 --> 36:49.582
Or do you know him somehow?

36:50.417 --> 36:54.129
Not at all.
I've never spoken to him before. Why?

36:54.212 --> 36:57.298
This is just my gut feeling.

36:59.426 --> 37:00.719
But I think he likes you.

37:00.802 --> 37:03.471
[sighs] What are you talking about?
That's so random.

37:04.931 --> 37:06.433
Did something happen?

37:06.516 --> 37:09.227
What? No, nothing happened.

37:09.728 --> 37:13.565
It's just that I sensed a romantic vibe.

37:13.648 --> 37:15.734
I told you that I've never spoken to him.

37:16.276 --> 37:17.652
By the way,

37:17.736 --> 37:20.655
I met Ho-su today.
He said he quit his job.

37:21.531 --> 37:23.324
What? He left the firm?

37:24.033 --> 37:26.745
But why did he suddenly show up there?

37:27.412 --> 37:30.206
I don't know. He said he wanted
to talk to me out of the blue.

37:30.290 --> 37:32.625
And he randomly started talking
about Dusonbong Peak.

37:32.709 --> 37:35.086
Dusonbong Peak? What about it?

37:35.170 --> 37:39.048
He just said
that it was a turning point in his life.

37:39.549 --> 37:41.009
He thanked you.

37:41.092 --> 37:43.303
He said he made it to the top
because of you.

37:44.012 --> 37:45.221
Because of me?

37:46.181 --> 37:48.850
Why did he randomly bring that up?

37:49.976 --> 37:51.186
Are you okay?

37:52.020 --> 37:54.439
It was a bit awkward.

37:55.023 --> 37:57.734
I was afraid
that he'd recognize me, but he didn't.

37:58.902 --> 38:00.153
That's not what I meant.

38:01.321 --> 38:03.865
I'm sorry you had to hear that.

38:04.741 --> 38:07.035
I know that you two dated in the past.

38:07.535 --> 38:08.620
[Mi-rae] What?

38:10.538 --> 38:12.290
Are you saying that because of that rumor?

38:12.373 --> 38:13.583
[exhales]

38:13.666 --> 38:18.838
You two came to my race that day,
and you were hugging.

38:19.464 --> 38:20.507
What?

38:23.760 --> 38:24.803
[sighs]

38:25.595 --> 38:27.555
You're talking about the day
you got hurt, right?

38:27.639 --> 38:29.182
I was sick that day.

38:30.308 --> 38:31.976
- You were sick?
- [intriguing music playing]

38:32.060 --> 38:34.145
95TH NATIONAL SPORTS CHAMPIONSHIP

38:34.229 --> 38:35.814
[Mi-rae] I wasn't feeling well,

38:35.897 --> 38:37.857
but I had an academic competition
that day.

38:37.941 --> 38:40.360
Honestly, I don't know
how I even managed to get there.

38:40.443 --> 38:41.861
The others are over there. Let's go.

38:41.945 --> 38:42.987
[sighs]

38:43.071 --> 38:45.657
What's wrong? Are you okay?

38:46.157 --> 38:48.368
I'm fine. It's okay.

38:48.910 --> 38:50.912
[pants]

38:54.332 --> 38:55.416
Mi-rae!

38:56.000 --> 38:57.585
Mi-rae, wake up! Hey!

38:58.711 --> 38:59.629
Hey!

38:59.712 --> 39:00.797
Don't tell them?

39:01.422 --> 39:04.050
Even if you don't want to,
you should tell them that you're sick.

39:04.133 --> 39:05.134
No.

39:06.511 --> 39:07.512
[sighs heavily]

39:07.595 --> 39:10.223
I'll be hospitalized
the moment my family finds out.

39:10.306 --> 39:12.433
I can't tell them until the CSAT is over.

39:12.517 --> 39:15.353
What's the point of taking the CSAT
when you're this sick?

39:15.436 --> 39:17.105
[breathes shakily]

39:17.188 --> 39:18.481
You know how it is.

39:20.066 --> 39:21.526
You know what it means.

39:22.819 --> 39:26.114
You know how crappy it feels
when your body doesn't listen to you.

39:27.615 --> 39:30.201
It's bad enough
that my own body won't listen to me.

39:31.661 --> 39:34.122
I don't need anything else
being out of my control.

39:35.915 --> 39:37.667
So… [breathes shakily]

39:39.210 --> 39:40.628
…don't tell anyone.

39:42.171 --> 39:43.423
Even Mi-ji.

39:44.883 --> 39:45.884
Why…

39:46.467 --> 39:48.678
- [music fades]
- Why didn't you tell me that?

39:49.387 --> 39:52.432
I just told you.
It was a secret until I took the CSAT.

39:52.515 --> 39:54.475
Ho-su didn't tell you after that?

39:55.101 --> 39:56.185
He didn't.

39:56.686 --> 40:00.899
Why didn't you tell me after the CSAT?

40:02.358 --> 40:04.360
You know how things were after the CSAT.

40:04.444 --> 40:07.071
How could I tell you
when you refused to even see me?

40:07.822 --> 40:09.115
[Mi-ji] But…

40:09.198 --> 40:11.868
You could've at least told me later.

40:11.951 --> 40:14.412
[Mi-rae] Why would I
when you never asked about it?

40:15.288 --> 40:18.082
And you were dating Gyeong-gu back then.

40:18.666 --> 40:21.169
I thought you weren't interested in Ho-su.

40:22.754 --> 40:24.672
Did you like him?

40:25.506 --> 40:26.591
No.

40:27.759 --> 40:31.220
Why did Ho-su send mixed signals?

40:32.347 --> 40:34.474
[Mi-rae] You confused him back then.

40:34.557 --> 40:35.755
[Mi-ji] What did I do?

40:35.832 --> 40:39.223
Who knew you'd suddenly
start dating Gyeong-gu?

40:39.298 --> 40:41.105
But Ho-su was very obvious
about his feelings.

40:41.189 --> 40:43.441
He even treated you and me differently.

40:44.067 --> 40:46.194
You had a feeling, didn't you?

40:46.819 --> 40:50.573
Then why was there a rumor
that you two were dating?

40:51.532 --> 40:54.202
[sighs] Is that so important?

40:54.285 --> 40:55.828
I told you it wasn't true.

40:55.912 --> 40:59.540
Is it my job to figure out why
people said that when it's not even true?

40:59.624 --> 41:00.667
No.

41:01.376 --> 41:03.544
That's not what I'm saying.

41:05.088 --> 41:07.590
Why are you suddenly getting upset?

41:11.135 --> 41:12.220
[sighs]

41:12.762 --> 41:14.430
I don't know why.

41:15.181 --> 41:17.850
People just saw what they wanted to
and spread rumors.

41:18.434 --> 41:19.727
[breathes deeply]

41:19.811 --> 41:22.814
Let's stop talking about this. I'm tired.

41:23.481 --> 41:26.734
Okay. Good night.

41:29.529 --> 41:30.613
[cell phone beeps]

41:30.697 --> 41:31.823
[sighs]

41:33.282 --> 41:34.701
[melancholic music playing]

41:34.784 --> 41:35.868
[sighs]

41:37.161 --> 41:38.621
[melancholic music continues]

41:39.372 --> 41:42.250
[Mi-ji panting, groaning]

41:49.549 --> 41:50.925
[groans]

41:52.093 --> 41:53.720
[Mi-ji] That was it?

41:53.803 --> 41:56.764
We ended up like this
over a simple misunderstanding?

41:56.848 --> 41:58.224
[exhales]

41:58.307 --> 42:00.935
I didn't have the courage
to ask about what happened,

42:01.811 --> 42:05.815
so I gave up on my life,
running, and even Ho-su.

42:06.733 --> 42:08.693
What have I been doing?

42:08.776 --> 42:10.653
[breathes deeply]

42:17.618 --> 42:19.871
[music concludes]

42:19.954 --> 42:21.372
Who had a lovers' quarrel?

42:21.456 --> 42:23.708
Mi-ji, Ok-hui's daughter.

42:25.168 --> 42:26.669
She's in a love triangle.

42:26.753 --> 42:28.504
A love triangle? With whom?

42:28.588 --> 42:31.591
You know, the mart owner's son
and the grandson from Changhwa Farm.

42:31.674 --> 42:34.135
They were arguing over Mi-ji.
[imitates growling]

42:35.762 --> 42:39.515
Gyeong-gu threw a fit, demanding
that Mi-ji give him some jam as well.

42:39.599 --> 42:42.101
He ended up on the floor
like a kid throwing a tantrum.

42:42.185 --> 42:43.895
My goodness, in front of everybody?

42:43.978 --> 42:47.815
Goodness, you know how it is
to get into a lovers' quarrel at that age.

42:47.899 --> 42:50.068
- [laughs] You're right…
- Oh my gosh!

42:50.693 --> 42:52.487
Who did she give the jam to?

42:53.154 --> 42:54.113
Pardon?

42:54.614 --> 42:55.865
Who was it?

43:00.703 --> 43:01.829
Enjoy.

43:02.371 --> 43:04.540
What is up with you? Jeez…

43:04.624 --> 43:06.459
Why are you smiling so much?

43:06.542 --> 43:08.878
It seems like the long winter is over

43:09.587 --> 43:13.007
and the flowers are in full bloom
for our dear Mi-ji.

43:13.091 --> 43:15.760
What are you talking about?

43:17.553 --> 43:20.014
I don't know if I should tell you this.

43:21.891 --> 43:25.520
- Whatever. I'm just going to tell you.
- I hope you enjoy your food.

43:25.603 --> 43:26.896
Mi-ji…

43:26.979 --> 43:28.397
[whispers] …has fallen in love.

43:28.481 --> 43:30.399
- What?
- [quirky music playing]

43:30.483 --> 43:33.820
- [giggles]
- Oh, I'm sorry. Enjoy.

43:35.488 --> 43:39.033
What in the world are you talking about?

43:39.117 --> 43:40.118
With whom?

43:40.201 --> 43:42.620
The strawberry farm owner
she's working with.

43:42.703 --> 43:46.082
When you work with someone,
you start developing feelings for them.

43:47.583 --> 43:50.086
That's how I met my husband.

43:50.753 --> 43:52.088
Don't say such ridiculous things.

43:52.171 --> 43:55.049
Why is that ridiculous?

43:55.758 --> 43:58.469
Mi-ji is 30 years old.
She should be dating at her age.

43:58.553 --> 44:01.472
And it seems like
she's found her calling these days.

44:01.556 --> 44:04.809
It would be nice if they got married
and worked on the farm together.

44:04.892 --> 44:07.728
Are you saying those awful things
because she's not your daughter?

44:07.812 --> 44:09.856
Mi-ji doesn't have a lot going for her,

44:09.939 --> 44:12.483
so I should just marry her off,
is that it?

44:12.567 --> 44:14.443
- What are you talking about?
- [Ok-hui] Jeez.

44:14.527 --> 44:16.445
Hey, what's wrong with getting married?

44:16.529 --> 44:20.032
I think getting married
was the best decision I ever made.

44:20.116 --> 44:23.286
If marriage is so wonderful,
then why not marry off your son?

44:23.911 --> 44:25.163
Switch places with me.

44:28.166 --> 44:29.125
[music concludes]

44:29.792 --> 44:33.546
[CEO] This is confidential,
so don't share it with anyone yet.

44:33.629 --> 44:34.797
NEW HQ
AND LRT LINE INTEGRATION

44:34.922 --> 44:36.048
The city has agreed to it.

44:36.132 --> 44:38.718
Whether the project proceeds
as planned depends on that building.

44:38.801 --> 44:40.052
What was it called again?

44:40.136 --> 44:42.388
- Rosa Restaurant, sir.
- [CEO] Right.

44:43.014 --> 44:45.850
The General Affairs Team told me
that there's been some progress.

44:45.933 --> 44:49.729
Yes, we're meeting with the landowner's
legal representative today.

44:49.812 --> 44:52.148
I heard the landowner
was giving us trouble.

44:52.231 --> 44:55.484
But I guess things worked out,
seeing as you're having a meeting.

44:55.568 --> 44:58.029
- Who's in charge of it?
- [intriguing quirky music playing]

44:58.112 --> 44:59.030
Me, sir.

44:59.113 --> 45:00.406
You're in charge?

45:00.489 --> 45:01.824
It's my department's job.

45:01.908 --> 45:04.660
So I should be responsible for it
from start to finish.

45:04.744 --> 45:07.079
Okay. I trust you'll do well.

45:07.163 --> 45:09.957
Do well on this,
and you may get promoted this time.

45:10.458 --> 45:12.585
Yes, I'll do my best.

45:17.465 --> 45:19.217
- Mr. Shin.
- Yes, sir.

45:19.300 --> 45:22.261
Please tell the General Affairs Team
not to attend today's meeting. I'll go.

45:22.345 --> 45:24.555
- [Gyeong-min] You're going, sir?
- Yes. Is the room ready?

45:24.639 --> 45:25.640
Uh…

45:26.307 --> 45:28.351
I was just about to…

45:28.976 --> 45:30.770
Why haven't you started yet?
Look at the time.

45:30.853 --> 45:32.438
Everyone, get the meeting room ready!

45:32.521 --> 45:34.482
Yes, sir. Get it ready.

45:37.109 --> 45:38.194
[music concludes]

45:38.277 --> 45:40.571
What's wrong with Director Choi today?

45:40.655 --> 45:41.989
What's he up to?

45:43.699 --> 45:46.953
[whispers] You don't have
any hacking skills, do you?

45:47.036 --> 45:49.038
I think I can go steal a cell phone.

45:50.122 --> 45:51.457
[scoffs]

45:53.417 --> 45:55.044
Wow…

45:55.878 --> 45:58.798
Mi-rae got her claws into a kid this time.

45:59.548 --> 46:02.551
[employee 1] If she's smart,
she should avoid married men.

46:02.635 --> 46:05.346
I'm sure she doesn't want
to get slapped again at Gwanghwamun.

46:05.429 --> 46:06.639
[employee 2] Right.

46:08.140 --> 46:11.060
[employee 1] How did she manage
to seduce that guy when he's like a robot?

46:11.143 --> 46:13.104
You know she's an expert at that.

46:13.187 --> 46:14.897
She pretends to have feelings for you,

46:14.981 --> 46:18.567
only to abandon you once you're useless
and then play the victim.

46:18.651 --> 46:21.696
Women like her
are a disgrace to the rest of us.

46:21.779 --> 46:23.239
[intriguing music playing]

46:23.322 --> 46:24.532
Do you know that statement

46:24.615 --> 46:27.785
could get you up to five years in prison
or a ten-million-won fine?

46:27.868 --> 46:28.744
Pardon?

46:28.828 --> 46:31.664
Publicly stating false facts
about a specific individual constitutes

46:31.747 --> 46:35.793
the crime of defamation under Article 307,
Paragraph 2 of the Criminal Act.

46:35.876 --> 46:39.505
If this falls under workplace harassment,
then a civil lawsuit may be possible too.

46:39.588 --> 46:43.301
We were just talking to each other.
How is that a public statement?

46:44.093 --> 46:45.803
But I heard you.

46:53.936 --> 46:56.272
- [employee 2] What the hell?
- [Mi-ji] Come in.

46:59.650 --> 47:01.027
- Oh. Ho-su--
- [music concludes]

47:01.110 --> 47:04.113
My name is Lee Ho-su.
I'm Ms. Ro-sa's legal representative.

47:04.196 --> 47:05.448
Where should I sit?

47:06.699 --> 47:09.118
Ah, okay.

47:09.201 --> 47:10.995
Please come this way.

47:15.166 --> 47:16.751
When you look at the first page--

47:16.834 --> 47:19.712
If you read it, I'm sure you'll see

47:19.795 --> 47:23.674
that the proposed amount is nearly 40%
higher than the local market average.

47:23.758 --> 47:25.051
Yes.

47:25.134 --> 47:27.178
As for the retail spaces
within the new headquarters--

47:27.261 --> 47:29.096
We also plan
to guarantee the landowner priority

47:29.180 --> 47:31.724
for leasing a retail space,
if that is her preference,

47:31.807 --> 47:34.435
so she may continue operating
her current restaurant.

47:40.232 --> 47:42.485
Exactly who is in charge of this matter?

47:43.110 --> 47:44.111
It's me.

47:48.449 --> 47:49.575
[Ho-su] Ah.

47:50.534 --> 47:52.870
So, you're Director Choi.

47:53.496 --> 47:55.956
It's the same proposal
you sent last time, isn't it?

47:57.208 --> 47:59.627
Yes. Probably.

48:00.169 --> 48:03.255
My client has stated that
she won't sell under these terms.

48:05.966 --> 48:10.096
From our standpoint, these terms
are already pushing the limits.

48:10.179 --> 48:13.391
Other landowners who've already sold
may even complain if they find out.

48:13.474 --> 48:16.185
Doesn't that mean that it's a site
that you need to secure,

48:16.268 --> 48:18.604
even if it means
you have to go beyond your limits?

48:19.313 --> 48:21.315
- Yes, then…
- [suspenseful music playing]

48:21.399 --> 48:23.567
Are there any additional terms
you would like?

48:23.651 --> 48:27.446
That's something you should propose.
Persuading the landowner isn't my job.

48:30.324 --> 48:34.370
I see. Then we'll continue
to visit her and…

48:34.453 --> 48:36.914
And my client feels uncomfortable

48:37.540 --> 48:41.877
with negotiations
that try to sway her emotionally

48:41.961 --> 48:43.546
through individual employees.

48:43.629 --> 48:46.799
From now on, I kindly request

48:47.842 --> 48:50.970
that only Director Choi, who is in charge,
convey the company's official stance

48:51.053 --> 48:53.848
directly through me,
Ms. Ro-sa's representative.

48:56.225 --> 48:57.893
Yes, of course. [exhales]

49:02.440 --> 49:03.941
[Tae-gwan exhales]

49:04.817 --> 49:05.860
[elevator chimes]

49:10.072 --> 49:12.533
[music builds]

49:12.616 --> 49:15.035
- [music concludes]
- [Mi-ji] Hey, Ho-su!

49:15.119 --> 49:16.287
Ho-su.

49:16.370 --> 49:18.330
You were just going to leave
without saying goodbye?

49:18.414 --> 49:19.540
Bye.

49:20.499 --> 49:23.169
Oh! That's all you have to say?

49:23.711 --> 49:26.755
Why did you follow me in here?
What if someone sees us?

49:26.839 --> 49:28.215
Who cares if they do?

49:28.299 --> 49:30.759
No good will come
from anyone seeing us together.

49:30.843 --> 49:32.970
Let's keep our personal
and work lives separate.

49:33.053 --> 49:37.516
Is that what you were doing
when you took my side earlier?

49:37.600 --> 49:39.143
[hesitates] What do you mean?

49:39.226 --> 49:40.853
Didn't you help me earlier?

49:41.854 --> 49:43.355
Why would I help you?

49:43.981 --> 49:47.568
Why are you suddenly getting annoyed?
I was just thanking you.

49:47.651 --> 49:48.986
[elevator chimes]

49:49.820 --> 49:50.821
[Mi-ji] Hey!

49:52.490 --> 49:55.034
What's wrong with him?

50:02.833 --> 50:04.251
[cell phone buzzes]

50:07.213 --> 50:09.340
TEA PARTY AT CHANGHWA FARM
TOMORROW AFTERNOON

50:10.132 --> 50:11.133
[chuckles softly]

50:20.851 --> 50:22.770
Who are you texting?

50:23.437 --> 50:24.438
The strawberry farm owner.

50:25.439 --> 50:27.983
[Bun-hong] Mi-ji has fallen in love.

50:28.067 --> 50:30.277
The strawberry farm owner
she's working with.

50:33.948 --> 50:37.701
How old is the strawberry farm owner?

50:37.785 --> 50:38.953
Is he pretty old?

50:39.828 --> 50:41.205
I've never asked, so I don't know.

50:41.288 --> 50:43.707
How could you not even ask that?

50:43.791 --> 50:44.917
Jeez.

50:47.253 --> 50:49.588
You need to be able
to take care of yourself

50:49.672 --> 50:51.423
before dating or getting married.

50:53.884 --> 50:56.387
Relying on a man
just because your future looks uncertain

50:56.470 --> 50:58.764
is one of the quickest ways
to ruin your life.

50:59.265 --> 51:02.476
You don't have to look far.
I'm living proof of what happens.

51:03.102 --> 51:04.812
Do you want to end up like me?

51:06.188 --> 51:08.190
Why are you suddenly talking about this?

51:10.609 --> 51:12.945
I hear you're seeing
the strawberry farm owner.

51:14.029 --> 51:16.156
No wonder you've stuck
with this job for so long!

51:16.240 --> 51:17.866
Is it because you're dating him?

51:21.412 --> 51:22.538
Are people saying that?

51:22.621 --> 51:26.208
Is it not true?
Is that just a false rumor?

51:28.377 --> 51:31.255
They're already saying I am,
so does my response even matter?

51:31.338 --> 51:34.508
Stop playing games with me.
Is it true or not?

51:35.175 --> 51:36.302
It's not true.

51:38.178 --> 51:39.513
It's not?

51:40.681 --> 51:44.476
[sighs] Jeez, I knew it.

51:44.560 --> 51:49.523
These ridiculous stories are made up
by people with nothing better to do.

51:49.607 --> 51:52.067
- Goodness.
- [Mi-rae] You believed them.

51:53.527 --> 51:55.279
I didn't believe them.

51:55.779 --> 51:58.574
It's just that there's never been a rumor
about you and a man before.

51:58.657 --> 52:01.368
So I thought there might be
something going on.

52:01.452 --> 52:04.246
[overlapping echoing chatter and laughter]

52:05.205 --> 52:07.166
- [chatter stops]
- [somber music playing]

52:07.249 --> 52:09.126
Mi-ji, why aren't you eating?

52:09.209 --> 52:11.378
[somber music continues]

52:12.254 --> 52:15.090
[hyperventilating]

52:22.723 --> 52:24.642
[breathes deeply]

52:34.610 --> 52:37.988
[music continues, turns ominous]

52:38.906 --> 52:41.950
[Tae-gwan] It's confidential information,
so make sure it doesn't get leaked.

52:42.034 --> 52:45.621
As you can tell, that restaurant
is the key to our new HQ project.

52:46.288 --> 52:49.583
But the landowner has suddenly appointed
a legal representative, so…

52:50.167 --> 52:55.339
But there's not much we can do
since the landowner doesn't want to sell.

52:55.422 --> 52:56.548
Oh?

52:56.632 --> 52:59.009
Her legal representative is Mr. Lee Ho-su.

52:59.093 --> 53:00.344
Do you know him?

53:00.427 --> 53:02.388
[lawyer] Yes,
he used to work at our law firm.

53:02.471 --> 53:05.683
Are you just looking for assistance
in purchasing Rosa Restaurant?

53:05.766 --> 53:08.310
Yes, do you have any way…

53:09.603 --> 53:12.481
Give me all the information
you have concerning this case.

53:13.857 --> 53:15.150
I'll take this on.

53:15.984 --> 53:17.111
[chuckles softly]

53:19.154 --> 53:20.531
[music concludes]

53:20.614 --> 53:22.324
[fire crackling]

53:22.408 --> 53:23.951
[whispers, in English] Okay, okay.

53:25.202 --> 53:26.328
[plate scrapes]

53:29.915 --> 53:31.667
[in Korean] Oh, welcome.

53:32.626 --> 53:33.836
Please come this way.

53:35.713 --> 53:37.172
Should I take your hat?

53:37.840 --> 53:38.882
I…

53:39.633 --> 53:40.718
I quit.

53:41.802 --> 53:44.304
I went overboard, didn't I? I'm sorry.

53:45.013 --> 53:46.181
Please have a seat.

53:49.768 --> 53:51.311
[soft music playing]

53:51.395 --> 53:54.273
Wait. You're really quitting?
Just like that?

53:55.691 --> 53:57.860
Why? Did I do something wrong?

53:58.527 --> 54:00.404
No, it's nothing like that.

54:01.363 --> 54:03.615
But you didn't say anything yesterday.

54:03.699 --> 54:06.493
We've just planted the strawberries,
and they're growing steadily.

54:06.577 --> 54:10.289
We also need to work on the tarp.
I can't do it all by myself.

54:11.415 --> 54:12.624
[Mi-rae] I'm sorry.

54:15.586 --> 54:16.670
Wait. Hold on.

54:19.298 --> 54:21.675
At least tell me why.

54:21.759 --> 54:25.220
Even if you're a temporary worker,
we've been working together for a while.

54:25.304 --> 54:28.307
- If you tell me the problem--
- [Mi-rae] It's my problem.

54:29.308 --> 54:31.101
Thank you for everything.

54:36.440 --> 54:37.775
[music fades]

54:42.070 --> 54:43.739
NEW HQ PROJECT REPORT

54:55.542 --> 54:58.462
Sir, here's the new HQ project report.

55:00.839 --> 55:01.757
[paper stack thuds]

55:14.144 --> 55:15.312
[scoffs]

55:17.356 --> 55:19.358
You did this on purpose, didn't you?

55:20.359 --> 55:21.360
Pardon?

55:21.443 --> 55:24.738
Look at these sentences. Hmm?

55:24.822 --> 55:26.949
[pensive music playing]

55:27.574 --> 55:29.451
The bullet points don't align either.

55:30.035 --> 55:33.747
All the tables have different units.
Some are in thousands and some aren't.

55:34.581 --> 55:36.625
And why didn't you cite your source here?

55:37.459 --> 55:39.837
Who submits a report like this to the CEO?

55:39.920 --> 55:42.339
Did you just wing this
because you didn't want to do it?

55:42.422 --> 55:44.091
Or is this the best you can do?

55:44.716 --> 55:47.636
I'm sorry. I was a bit careless
because I was in a hurry.

55:47.719 --> 55:49.763
You were careless? So you did wing this?

55:53.892 --> 55:54.768
Take it.

55:55.853 --> 55:57.813
I'm sorry. I'll fix it right away and--

55:57.896 --> 55:59.022
[Gyeong-min] Forget it.

55:59.106 --> 56:02.276
I'll fix it, so give me
the original file and the raw data.

56:02.359 --> 56:04.194
You should've just passed this
onto me sooner.

56:04.278 --> 56:05.654
What were you doing until now?

56:06.321 --> 56:08.490
Are you trying to make my life harder?

56:08.574 --> 56:09.533
Go.

56:13.161 --> 56:15.539
[pensive music continues]

56:18.458 --> 56:19.710
[Gyeong-min sighs]

56:32.890 --> 56:34.683
RAW DATA
UNPROCESSED DATA

56:38.770 --> 56:40.480
[music fades]

56:40.564 --> 56:43.650
I WILL BE TAKING A SHORT BREAK
DUE TO HEALTH ISSUES

56:43.734 --> 56:44.693
[Ho-su] Yes, ma'am.

56:46.028 --> 56:48.530
I took a look around the restaurant.
Everything is fine.

56:48.614 --> 56:51.158
Don't worry.
I hope your surgery goes well tomorrow.

56:51.241 --> 56:52.910
- After the surgery, I…
- [knocking on door]

56:52.993 --> 56:54.703
[door sliding open]

56:54.786 --> 56:57.331
[Ji-yun] Is the restaurant closed again?

56:57.831 --> 57:00.083
Yes, the owner is sick, so…

57:00.751 --> 57:01.835
Ho-su.

57:13.430 --> 57:14.681
Thanks.

57:17.684 --> 57:19.937
- Thanks for the drink.
- Try this.

57:20.020 --> 57:21.438
This is their signature drink.

57:21.521 --> 57:22.731
It's okay. I'll drink this…

57:22.814 --> 57:25.025
[Ji-yun] Come on. Give that to me.

57:25.108 --> 57:27.653
This is my drink. Hurry up and try it.

57:33.617 --> 57:35.661
- [coughs]
- [chuckles]

57:35.744 --> 57:37.871
Hmm. It's good.

57:39.164 --> 57:41.583
You always drink Americanos, don't you?

57:41.667 --> 57:44.544
Drinks like this are fun.
You should try them sometimes.

57:45.212 --> 57:47.506
Anyway, why did you come
to the restaurant?

57:47.589 --> 57:48.840
- For work?
- [Ji-yun] Yes.

57:49.383 --> 57:51.301
Our next theme is retro.

57:51.385 --> 57:53.720
I went there a few times
to bring Ms. Ro-sa on board.

57:53.804 --> 57:56.139
I never expected to see you there, Ho-su.

57:56.807 --> 57:58.266
Did Mi-rae ask for your help?

58:00.519 --> 58:02.187
- Mi-rae?
- [Ji-yun] Yes.

58:02.270 --> 58:04.314
Didn't she ask for your help
because she was busy?

58:04.398 --> 58:06.400
Mi-rae's great-aunt runs that place.

58:07.234 --> 58:09.403
- Great-aunt?
- Yes.

58:10.696 --> 58:12.030
You didn't know?

58:12.656 --> 58:13.657
[scoffs]

58:14.282 --> 58:15.409
I didn't know.

58:16.410 --> 58:18.578
I'm the owner's legal representative.

58:20.038 --> 58:21.164
I see.

58:23.000 --> 58:25.544
I just assumed you were there
because of Mi-rae.

58:25.627 --> 58:26.795
Why?

58:27.587 --> 58:28.755
It's not like that.

58:29.548 --> 58:32.259
Well, you two are always together.

58:32.759 --> 58:35.262
And you also arrived
at the high school reunion together.

58:35.345 --> 58:38.974
Plus, back in the day, there was a rumor
that you two were dating.

58:41.476 --> 58:43.645
I wanted to ask you about that.

58:44.479 --> 58:46.189
Why did that rumor start?

58:46.273 --> 58:47.691
That's because…

58:48.358 --> 58:52.070
you two gave off similar vibes
and you seemed so alike.

58:52.696 --> 58:55.574
You always hung out together
and skipped school on the same days.

58:55.657 --> 58:59.411
That's because we were the only ones
in the academic competition prep class…

59:01.079 --> 59:02.122
Anyway, we didn't date.

59:09.629 --> 59:11.131
Then what about now?

59:12.090 --> 59:14.217
- What do you think of Mi-rae now?
- [coughs]

59:15.677 --> 59:17.471
[soft pensive music playing]

59:17.554 --> 59:19.056
Are you interested in anyone?

59:24.311 --> 59:26.229
[soft pensive music continues]

59:33.779 --> 59:34.863
[exhales]

59:49.669 --> 59:51.379
[Mi-ji breathing deeply]

59:54.633 --> 59:56.593
[Tae-i] What are you doing by yourself?

59:57.511 --> 59:58.553
Oh…

59:59.137 --> 01:00:01.056
- [music fades]
- [Mi-ji chuckles softly]

01:00:03.058 --> 01:00:05.602
[slurring] I'm so sorry that things
turned out this way

01:00:05.685 --> 01:00:07.604
even after you helped me.

01:00:19.783 --> 01:00:22.160
Why did you do that earlier?

01:00:23.453 --> 01:00:24.579
What do you mean?

01:00:26.540 --> 01:00:27.624
The report…

01:00:28.750 --> 01:00:30.252
You didn't wing it.

01:00:32.838 --> 01:00:36.508
You worked hard on it
day and night, so why…

01:00:38.969 --> 01:00:41.054
I didn't want him to know.

01:00:43.974 --> 01:00:44.975
Know what?

01:00:47.853 --> 01:00:49.729
That I did my best.

01:00:51.481 --> 01:00:54.860
If that were the best I could do,

01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:58.572
I'd feel so small and pathetic.

01:00:59.364 --> 01:01:01.074
- [inhales deeply]
- [soft music playing]

01:01:01.158 --> 01:01:03.869
That's why I lied
about not giving it my all.

01:01:04.828 --> 01:01:09.499
I thought it'd be better for him
to think I'm lazy than incompetent.

01:01:11.459 --> 01:01:15.130
[sighs] Even though I made a promise…

01:01:22.304 --> 01:01:25.056
You're not yourself right now, though.

01:01:27.225 --> 01:01:30.145
But you managed to do all that on your own
despite what you're going through.

01:01:30.228 --> 01:01:32.105
- [glass sets down]
- I know, right?

01:01:32.731 --> 01:01:34.149
To be honest,

01:01:34.232 --> 01:01:38.236
it's a miracle that I managed
to even make that report.

01:01:38.320 --> 01:01:40.906
But no one knows that.

01:01:41.573 --> 01:01:42.616
Yes.

01:01:43.617 --> 01:01:46.036
They shouldn't know.

01:01:48.955 --> 01:01:50.790
If you're having a hard time…

01:01:50.874 --> 01:01:51.833
[sighs]

01:01:51.917 --> 01:01:53.793
…why don't you take a short break?

01:01:54.336 --> 01:01:57.881
If you rest a little
and take some time for yourself…

01:01:57.964 --> 01:01:59.382
[inhales sharply]

01:02:00.300 --> 01:02:02.177
Absolutely not.

01:02:02.677 --> 01:02:05.138
That's really dangerous.

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:08.600
That's how I ended up
holing myself up in my room.

01:02:10.060 --> 01:02:11.061
Holed up?

01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:12.771
Don't even get me started.

01:02:13.313 --> 01:02:17.234
Once you go in there,
it's so hard to come out.

01:02:19.402 --> 01:02:21.154
So how did you get out?

01:02:22.906 --> 01:02:24.699
How did I get out?

01:02:26.701 --> 01:02:27.953
[chuckles softly]

01:02:29.079 --> 01:02:30.705
My grandma…

01:02:32.290 --> 01:02:34.084
asked for me.

01:02:35.835 --> 01:02:36.836
[Ok-hui] Mi-ji.

01:02:36.920 --> 01:02:38.171
[soft music continues]

01:02:38.922 --> 01:02:40.173
Mi-ji.

01:02:41.383 --> 01:02:43.843
Grandma keeps asking for you.

01:02:45.095 --> 01:02:47.806
She can't even walk now.

01:02:47.889 --> 01:02:49.557
[breathes shakily]

01:02:51.893 --> 01:02:53.937
She's bedridden.

01:02:55.981 --> 01:02:57.482
You need to go see her.

01:03:00.485 --> 01:03:03.113
She said she has something to tell you.

01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:07.784
So she'll be waiting for your visit.

01:03:08.410 --> 01:03:10.787
[breathing deeply]

01:03:13.081 --> 01:03:14.708
[sniffles, sobs]

01:03:16.876 --> 01:03:22.048
I somehow managed to go out
on the day she collapsed.

01:03:22.132 --> 01:03:23.800
[music fades]

01:03:23.883 --> 01:03:25.969
But I couldn't bring myself

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:28.596
to keep going out
just because I did it once.

01:03:28.680 --> 01:03:30.140
I was such an idiot.

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:32.517
[Mi-ji breathing shakily]

01:03:40.150 --> 01:03:42.569
[sobs]

01:03:45.322 --> 01:03:47.115
But all of a sudden,

01:03:48.700 --> 01:03:51.244
for some reason, I thought of someone.

01:03:51.328 --> 01:03:52.704
[young Ho-su] I felt that…

01:03:53.246 --> 01:03:54.372
[melancholic music playing]

01:03:54.456 --> 01:03:56.791
…if I couldn't even climb
a mountain like this,

01:03:57.625 --> 01:03:59.085
then I would rather die.

01:04:00.295 --> 01:04:01.921
[Mi-ji sobs, sniffles]

01:04:02.630 --> 01:04:05.216
So I thought to myself,

01:04:06.634 --> 01:04:12.182
"If I can't even go see Grandma today…

01:04:14.559 --> 01:04:16.603
then I should just die."

01:04:16.686 --> 01:04:19.731
[sobbing] Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:04:19.814 --> 01:04:21.983
Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:04:22.067 --> 01:04:24.736
Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:04:24.819 --> 01:04:26.821
Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:04:26.905 --> 01:04:29.032
Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:30.784
And so…

01:04:36.039 --> 01:04:39.000
A trip that would usually take me
30 minutes on foot…

01:04:40.543 --> 01:04:41.586
It…

01:04:42.504 --> 01:04:43.671
took me…

01:04:46.299 --> 01:04:49.010
four hours for me to get to her.

01:04:51.221 --> 01:04:52.847
[music turns uplifting]

01:05:03.191 --> 01:05:05.485
[breathes shakily]

01:05:20.083 --> 01:05:21.251
[weakly] Oh!

01:05:21.334 --> 01:05:23.044
Grandma!

01:05:26.631 --> 01:05:28.007
Grandma!

01:05:28.758 --> 01:05:31.678
- Grandma…
- [Wol-sun] My goodness, sweetie.

01:05:31.761 --> 01:05:34.514
I knew you'd come.

01:05:34.597 --> 01:05:38.393
[stuttering] I knew you would, sweetie.

01:05:38.476 --> 01:05:41.563
I'm sorry, Grandma. It's my fault.

01:05:42.772 --> 01:05:45.358
[Wol-sun] It's not your fault, Mi-ji.

01:05:45.900 --> 01:05:50.405
I asked you to come
so I could tell you that.

01:05:53.700 --> 01:05:57.620
Now that I'm bedridden,

01:05:57.704 --> 01:06:00.248
I finally understand how you feel.

01:06:01.207 --> 01:06:04.752
[sobbing] I'm old, but I'm scared too.

01:06:06.129 --> 01:06:10.967
So I can only imagine how scary
and difficult it must've been for you.

01:06:12.385 --> 01:06:14.137
- [sobs]
- [Wol-sun] But you know,

01:06:14.929 --> 01:06:18.516
I've realized something
now that you're here.

01:06:18.600 --> 01:06:21.394
Just like your name means "unknown,"

01:06:23.229 --> 01:06:25.190
we don't know yet.

01:06:25.273 --> 01:06:26.274
[sobs]

01:06:26.357 --> 01:06:31.488
[Wol-sun] Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:06:32.113 --> 01:06:37.118
But today is yet unknown, Mi-ji.

01:06:37.785 --> 01:06:39.329
So…

01:06:40.538 --> 01:06:44.167
let's live today.

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:50.089
I'll do my best to live somehow.

01:06:50.173 --> 01:06:52.425
So I want you to live too.

01:06:52.509 --> 01:06:55.512
[Mi-ji] Yes…

01:06:56.971 --> 01:07:00.558
Promise me…

01:07:01.518 --> 01:07:04.062
that you'll never run away from anything.

01:07:04.687 --> 01:07:05.939
Promise me…

01:07:07.398 --> 01:07:08.816
now.

01:07:09.359 --> 01:07:10.610
[sobs]

01:07:10.693 --> 01:07:15.490
[Wol-sun] Together,
let's endure one day at a time.

01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:19.452
[sobbing] Yes.

01:07:27.752 --> 01:07:29.254
- [sniffles]
- [uplifting music continues]

01:07:29.337 --> 01:07:30.964
From that day,

01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:38.930
I've endured one day at a time
and made it to today.

01:07:42.517 --> 01:07:44.227
- I had no idea.
- [music concludes]

01:07:45.103 --> 01:07:47.105
I didn't know you'd been through so much.

01:07:47.188 --> 01:07:49.566
[chuckles] What's the point, though?

01:07:50.400 --> 01:07:53.278
I promised her
that I wouldn't run away from anything.

01:07:54.404 --> 01:07:56.781
But I broke that promise today.

01:07:58.408 --> 01:07:59.909
You didn't break your promise.

01:08:00.451 --> 01:08:03.496
You didn't run away,
and you submitted the report.

01:08:03.997 --> 01:08:05.540
I lied.

01:08:07.792 --> 01:08:09.085
I could've just said,

01:08:09.794 --> 01:08:11.421
"I'm sorry."

01:08:12.088 --> 01:08:14.173
"Even though I did my best,

01:08:15.550 --> 01:08:18.469
this is all I can do."

01:08:20.597 --> 01:08:23.808
But… I lied.

01:08:26.436 --> 01:08:28.229
No one knows that, though.

01:08:29.731 --> 01:08:30.857
That you lied.

01:08:31.608 --> 01:08:33.109
But I know.

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:36.404
[pensive music playing]

01:08:36.487 --> 01:08:40.992
To be honest, I got a bit hopeful today.

01:08:41.534 --> 01:08:42.577
[sniffles]

01:08:43.119 --> 01:08:46.205
It's been a while since I've put
all my effort into something.

01:08:47.332 --> 01:08:49.500
I should've expected
that I wouldn't do well.

01:08:51.794 --> 01:08:53.755
But I really wanted to do a good job.

01:08:57.050 --> 01:08:59.636
So I guess I didn't want to find out

01:09:01.346 --> 01:09:02.889
that this is all I am.

01:09:05.475 --> 01:09:06.851
[voice trembling] But…

01:09:08.227 --> 01:09:10.396
I can't fool myself.

01:09:11.022 --> 01:09:12.065
[sniffles]

01:09:12.899 --> 01:09:15.318
I should just accept it.

01:09:16.736 --> 01:09:18.112
But I can't.

01:09:20.490 --> 01:09:24.077
That's why I've spent my whole life
running away like this. I'm an idiot.

01:09:26.913 --> 01:09:28.956
[sobs]

01:09:30.041 --> 01:09:32.001
[pensive music continues]

01:09:32.669 --> 01:09:36.089
[Mi-ji sobbing]

01:09:45.181 --> 01:09:47.266
[music fades]

01:09:50.269 --> 01:09:51.854
[Ho-su] Thank you for the ride.

01:09:53.231 --> 01:09:54.482
I'll see you later.

01:09:54.565 --> 01:09:55.858
Wait, Ho-su.

01:09:58.945 --> 01:09:59.946
Here.

01:10:02.031 --> 01:10:03.199
And this too.

01:10:05.702 --> 01:10:07.870
What's all this?

01:10:07.954 --> 01:10:11.082
I collected these souvenirs
from the restaurants I covered.

01:10:11.165 --> 01:10:13.418
There's a lot of interesting food,
so try one at a time.

01:10:13.501 --> 01:10:14.961
You didn't have to.

01:10:15.878 --> 01:10:16.921
Thanks.

01:10:18.589 --> 01:10:20.049
How was today?

01:10:21.426 --> 01:10:25.972
Didn't you have fun going to new places
and trying new foods with me today?

01:10:26.848 --> 01:10:29.934
Yes, I got to experience new things,
thanks to you.

01:10:30.601 --> 01:10:31.686
Then…

01:10:32.353 --> 01:10:34.731
can I call you again?

01:10:35.648 --> 01:10:39.277
You don't need my permission for that.

01:10:39.360 --> 01:10:40.486
[chuckles]

01:10:41.028 --> 01:10:42.613
Let's see each other again.

01:10:43.156 --> 01:10:46.826
I'll make sure that you have
a really good time, Ho-su.

01:10:50.747 --> 01:10:52.415
[door lock beeping]

01:10:52.498 --> 01:10:54.333
- [door opens]
- [door lock chimes]

01:10:56.502 --> 01:10:58.296
- [door closes]
- [Tae-i] I'm home.

01:10:59.172 --> 01:11:00.423
[door lock chimes]

01:11:04.969 --> 01:11:06.846
[suspenseful music playing]

01:11:07.930 --> 01:11:09.599
About Ms. Yu…

01:11:11.017 --> 01:11:12.727
I think I should keep helping her.

01:11:15.188 --> 01:11:17.857
I think I have to.

01:11:27.575 --> 01:11:29.494
[suspenseful music continues]

01:11:33.080 --> 01:11:34.248
[music concludes]

01:11:35.291 --> 01:11:37.668
PLEATED SEA SQUIRT SSAM-JEOT

01:11:38.503 --> 01:11:39.420
MINT CHOCOLATE HIGHBALL

01:11:41.464 --> 01:11:43.132
[cell phone buzzing]

01:11:43.216 --> 01:11:45.927
YU MI-RAE

01:11:48.513 --> 01:11:50.723
[cell phone continues buzzing]

01:11:58.356 --> 01:11:59.774
MISSED CALL
YU MI-RAE

01:12:01.609 --> 01:12:03.069
[cell phone buzzing]

01:12:03.152 --> 01:12:05.696
YU MI-RAE

01:12:11.786 --> 01:12:12.787
What is it?

01:12:13.412 --> 01:12:16.457
[Mi-ji slurring] Hey! Ho-su!

01:12:16.541 --> 01:12:17.792
Come out!

01:12:17.875 --> 01:12:20.545
[quirky music playing]

01:12:22.630 --> 01:12:25.174
[Mi-ji elongating] Ho-su…

01:12:26.342 --> 01:12:28.594
Come out.

01:12:29.345 --> 01:12:30.680
Hello?

01:12:30.763 --> 01:12:32.306
- Mi-rae.
- Where…

01:12:33.391 --> 01:12:34.559
[Mi-ji] Oh?

01:12:35.768 --> 01:12:37.812
You…

01:12:37.895 --> 01:12:39.063
Oh, hey!

01:12:40.356 --> 01:12:41.691
[music concludes]

01:12:41.774 --> 01:12:43.484
Why are you so drunk?

01:12:43.568 --> 01:12:45.653
Jeez. Hey.

01:12:46.237 --> 01:12:49.991
When a woman's dealing
with work and life,

01:12:50.074 --> 01:12:53.160
there are days
when you get drunk like this,

01:12:53.244 --> 01:12:56.789
and there are days when you get upset.

01:12:56.873 --> 01:13:00.084
You should've gone home if you were drunk.
Why did you come here?

01:13:00.167 --> 01:13:01.627
Why, you little…

01:13:01.711 --> 01:13:05.715
Hey, Ho-su. Are you going
to keep treating me like this?

01:13:06.465 --> 01:13:07.967
What did I do?

01:13:08.050 --> 01:13:09.343
[Mi-ji] Hmm…

01:13:09.927 --> 01:13:12.138
You jerk.

01:13:12.680 --> 01:13:16.225
You keep confusing me,
sending me mixed signals.

01:13:16.309 --> 01:13:17.643
When did I ever do that?

01:13:17.727 --> 01:13:19.437
"When did I ever do that?"

01:13:19.520 --> 01:13:20.938
My gosh.

01:13:21.439 --> 01:13:24.150
- [tender music playing]
- Hey, you know what?

01:13:24.233 --> 01:13:27.987
I found it a bit odd when you started
talking about your first love.

01:13:28.070 --> 01:13:29.739
If you like Mi-ji,

01:13:29.822 --> 01:13:33.284
why can't you just tell me
why you like her?

01:13:33.784 --> 01:13:36.454
Why were you going on
about Dusonbong Peak instead?

01:13:36.537 --> 01:13:38.956
Are you playing Twenty Questions
with me right now?

01:13:39.916 --> 01:13:41.000
Why…

01:13:41.918 --> 01:13:43.252
are you curious about that?

01:13:43.878 --> 01:13:47.089
You made me curious.

01:13:47.173 --> 01:13:48.799
Hey, and another thing…

01:13:49.425 --> 01:13:53.012
You definitely went up
to Dusonbong Peak by yourself.

01:13:53.512 --> 01:13:54.889
So…

01:13:54.972 --> 01:13:57.475
So how could you have fallen for her
when you were going up?

01:13:57.558 --> 01:14:00.478
What do you mean by that?

01:14:00.561 --> 01:14:01.938
You really…

01:14:03.314 --> 01:14:05.816
Explain yourself.

01:14:06.859 --> 01:14:12.031
Explain exactly what you meant.

01:14:12.114 --> 01:14:13.616
Jeez…

01:14:13.699 --> 01:14:15.201
[music concludes]

01:14:15.284 --> 01:14:16.494
[sighs]

01:14:17.536 --> 01:14:18.537
Well?

01:14:25.002 --> 01:14:26.420
Mi-ji wasn't there.

01:14:28.965 --> 01:14:30.007
What?

01:14:30.508 --> 01:14:32.802
[soft pensive music playing]

01:14:33.844 --> 01:14:35.096
[Ho-su] That day…

01:14:36.639 --> 01:14:39.225
- I was the last one to the top.
- [student 1] Hang in there, Ho-su.

01:14:39.308 --> 01:14:42.061
You're doing great.
You're almost there, Ho-su.

01:14:42.144 --> 01:14:45.106
- [Ho-su] I was the only one going up.
- Hang in there, Ho-su.

01:14:46.273 --> 01:14:47.942
[student 2] Just a little more, Ho-su.

01:14:48.025 --> 01:14:49.443
[student 3] You're almost there.

01:14:49.527 --> 01:14:52.238
[Ho-su] Later on,
I saw no one else coming down.

01:14:52.321 --> 01:14:53.698
And I was alone.

01:14:55.282 --> 01:14:57.034
To be honest, I was so tired.

01:14:57.702 --> 01:15:00.663
I thought about giving up
and going back down several times.

01:15:01.664 --> 01:15:03.541
But I kept going up…

01:15:04.834 --> 01:15:06.419
because I didn't see Mi-ji…

01:15:07.586 --> 01:15:09.046
among the people coming down.

01:15:13.551 --> 01:15:15.177
[tender music playing]

01:15:15.261 --> 01:15:17.388
[Ho-su]
I didn't even have faith in myself.

01:15:20.182 --> 01:15:22.810
But she kept waiting,
believing that I'd come.

01:15:23.936 --> 01:15:25.396
That's what Mi-ji did for me.

01:15:56.260 --> 01:15:57.553
[tender music continues]

01:15:58.429 --> 01:16:00.181
[Ho-su] I went up there because of Mi-ji.

01:16:00.264 --> 01:16:03.142
If I'd been alone,
I would've never made it to the top.

01:16:04.435 --> 01:16:06.395
That's why I fell for her,

01:16:06.979 --> 01:16:09.398
because I kept thinking about her
while I was going up.

01:16:10.900 --> 01:16:12.068
Me too.

01:16:14.153 --> 01:16:15.446
You… What?

01:16:16.113 --> 01:16:17.990
[music fades]

01:16:18.657 --> 01:16:21.160
I went out that day
because I was thinking about you.

01:16:25.289 --> 01:16:26.415
I…

01:16:29.293 --> 01:16:30.961
I liked you too.

01:16:31.045 --> 01:16:33.464
[gentle pop song playing]

01:16:33.547 --> 01:16:39.428
[singing in Korean]

01:16:39.512 --> 01:16:45.518
[singing continues in Korean]

01:16:45.601 --> 01:16:48.437
[singing continues in Korean]

01:16:48.521 --> 01:16:53.400
[singing continues in Korean]

01:16:53.484 --> 01:16:56.570
[singing continues in Korean]

01:16:57.863 --> 01:17:02.326
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:03.452 --> 01:17:08.415
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:10.209 --> 01:17:14.880
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:15.881 --> 01:17:19.510
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:19.593 --> 01:17:20.761
YU MI-JI

01:17:20.845 --> 01:17:23.556
[Chung-gu]
Who's in charge of Rosa Restaurant?

01:17:23.639 --> 01:17:25.724
About the new HQ project.
I heard you might step down.

01:17:25.808 --> 01:17:29.728
If I took him out of the picture,
would you take the lead?

01:17:29.812 --> 01:17:32.982
[Ok-hui] It's just that she's been
down all day. She even quit the farm.

01:17:33.065 --> 01:17:35.568
Why don't you take her out
for some fresh air or something?

01:17:35.651 --> 01:17:37.444
You basically kidnapped me in your car.

01:17:37.528 --> 01:17:39.405
You really shouldn't cross the line.

01:17:39.488 --> 01:17:41.073
You're not Mi-ji, are you?

01:17:41.157 --> 01:17:42.491
What do you think of Ho-su?

01:17:42.575 --> 01:17:44.243
I want to give it a shot with him.

01:17:44.326 --> 01:17:46.328
[Mi-ji] It's like I've lost
before the fight began.

01:17:46.412 --> 01:17:48.914
Who are you going to go see?
She's not Mi-rae.

01:17:48.998 --> 01:17:51.375
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:51.458 --> 01:17:55.754
[singing continues in Korean]

01:17:56.255 --> 01:17:58.257
Subtitle translation by Jane Jung
